GS1 Barcode Syntax Dictionary — vendored third-party data
=========================================================

This directory contains an unmodified copy of the machine-readable GS1
Barcode Syntax Dictionary, which drives the M1 data-layer checks in
`src/bpreflight/gs1/dictionary.py`. The AI table is **read as data**; it is
never hand-transcribed into code (see `plan/00` decision D1).

Files
-----

  gs1-syntax-dictionary.txt   the AI table (unmodified upstream copy)
  LICENSE                     Apache License 2.0 (upstream copy)

Upstream
--------

  Repository  https://github.com/gs1/gs1-syntax-dictionary
  Source path gs1-syntax-dictionary.txt
  Snapshot    commit c63d8a12210dd0cfaceac4aae45ccf57b48eb15b
              (committed 2026-08-29T06:07:59Z)
  Retrieved   2026-10-27
  License     Apache License 2.0

The upstream file carries `# Release: UNSET` in its header, i.e. the tree is
not at a tagged release. That is why the pinned identifier used by this
project (`dict_version`, see `src/bpreflight/data/vectors/dict_manifest.json`)
is derived from the commit sha plus the snapshot date rather than from an
upstream version string.

  dict_version = gs1-syntax-dictionary@c63d8a12210d-2026-08-29

Integrity
---------

  sha256(gs1-syntax-dictionary.txt)
    = 1ea02f4e3b81d3092e095987600e01c7fd55310f4da5181f5a070262ff6ffc94

The same digest is recorded in `src/bpreflight/data/vectors/dict_manifest.json`
and is re-verified on every run by `src/bpreflight/gs1/dictionary.py`; a
mismatch raises `DictionaryError`, which the CLI maps to exit code 3
("bundled dictionary missing or altered"). It is also recomputable by hand:

  py -3.12 -c "import hashlib,io;print(hashlib.sha256(io.open('src/bpreflight/data/gs1-syntax-dictionary/gs1-syntax-dictionary.txt','rb').read()).hexdigest())"

