Rules transcribed from the upstream reference linter sources
------------------------------------------------------------

The four semantic interpreters implemented in `src/bpreflight/gs1/validators.py`
and the check-digit routine in `src/bpreflight/gs1/checksum.py` follow the
upstream C reference implementations that live in the same snapshot under
`src/lint_*.c`:

  lint_csum.c        numeric check digit: weight starts at 3 when the length
                     *including* the check digit is even, otherwise 1, then
                     alternates left-to-right (the other weight is 4 - W);
                     only data positions are summed; check = (10 - sum % 10) % 10
  lint_yymmd0.c      YYMMDD, additionally permitting YYMM00 (unspecified day);
                     uses a CURRENT_YEAR horizon to expand YY to a full year
  lint_yyyymmd0.c    YYYYMMDD / YYYYMM00; month must be 01..12; day is compared
                     against a leap-year-aware maximum, and DD = 00 is permitted
  lint_cset82.c      CSET 82: !"%&'()*+,-./0-9:;<=>?A-Z_a-z
  lint_cset39.c      CSET 39: #-/0-9A-Z
  lint_csetnumeric.c digits only

Those reference files are not copied into this repository (only the AI table
is vendored data); they remain fetchable from the upstream repository at the
commit pinned above.
